.config/opencode/commands

# Orphaned compound-engineering skills. They used to be fetched into
# ~/.agents/skills/ by the dotagents `[[skills]] name = "*"` wildcard entry;
# that entry is gone, because the plugin is now installed natively per agent
# (see the compound-engineering section in AGENTS.md). dotagents does NOT prune
# skill directories it no longer declares — its lock file drops them but the
# dirs stay, and its `sync` cannot run here at all (the chezmoi-managed
# ~/.agents/agents.toml is 0400, so sync's rewrite of it EACCESes). Left behind,
# every ce-* skill would load TWICE: once as a stale directory here and once
# from the plugin.
#
# Safe: these `ce-*` / `lfg` patterns match neither the external skills deployed
# there (`playwright-cli`, `improve`) nor the locally-authored chezmoi-managed
# skills under dot_agents/skills/<name>/ (`daily-report`); dotagents will never
# re-create the ce-* dirs now that the wildcard entry is gone.
.agents/skills/ce-*
.agents/skills/lfg

# Removed hub + its @AGENTS.md mirror. The user-scoped instruction core is now
# composed per harness by .chezmoitemplates/agents-instructions.tmpl and rendered
# straight into each harness wrapper (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, ~/.codex/AGENTS.md,
# ~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md, ~/.gemini/GEMINI.md, ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md), so
# the shared ~/.agents/AGENTS.md hub and its ~/.agents/CLAUDE.md mirror no longer
# have a source. Deleting the dot_agents source files stops managing them but
# does not delete the already-deployed copies — prune them here.
.agents/AGENTS.md
.agents/CLAUDE.md

# omp reads ~/.omp/agent/AGENTS.md natively and never CLAUDE.md, so the sibling
# @AGENTS.md mirror that dot_omp/private_agent/readonly_CLAUDE.md used to deploy
# was pointless: the mirror rule is a repository-documentation convention, not a
# managed-target one (see the managed instruction targets paragraph in
# AGENTS.md). Deleting that source stops managing the file but leaves the
# already-deployed 0444 copy behind — prune it here.
.omp/agent/CLAUDE.md

# Leftovers from the removed CLIProxyAPI binary integration (the 2026-07-21
# removal was source-only). The revival runs as a Podman quadlet on Linux and a
# launchd agent on macOS, so the old systemd user unit (linux-only) and the old
# shared launcher (darwin-only now) must not linger: a surviving unit would bind
# 127.0.0.1:8317 first at login and silently re-adopt stale OAuth credentials.
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "linux" }}
.config/systemd/user/cli-proxy-api.service
{{- end }}
{{- if ne .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}
.local/libexec/cli-proxy-api-launch
{{- end }}

# The garden project registry moved from ~/src/garden.yaml to
# ~/.config/garden/garden.yaml so ~/src holds only project trees. Deleting the
# old source stops managing the old target but leaves the already-deployed 0444
# copy behind — prune it here, in the target-application phase, so no stale
# registry is visible to the 90-src reconcile script that runs last.
src/garden.yaml
